    sections: [{"id":"sec-overview","heading":"What it is","body":"Versatile midplus Speed frame for players who want speed through the court.\n\nHead Speed MP 2024 is built for a specific job in the category — use that job as your first filter.\n\nI'd shortlist it when you want all-court versatility or accessible handling.\n\nI'd pause if not the stiffest plow-through option would show up often in your week.\n\nBottom line: Versatile midplus Speed frame for players who want speed through the court. I'd shortlist it when you want all-court versatility. I'd pause if not the stiffest plow-through option shows up often in your week.","evidenceIds":["ev-racket-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-verified-specs","heading":"Key specs","body":"Here are the numbers that matter for the Head Speed MP 2024:\n\n• Balance: even\n• Head Size: 100 in²\n• Strung Weight: 315 g\n• String Pattern: 16x19\n• Power Positioning: balanced\n• playerLevel: intermediate\n\nWeight and stack shape how protective or lively a shoe feels; drop and geometry change the transition; stability and terrain labels tell you the intended job; width options change who can wear it. For watches and other gear, treat battery, sensors and materials the same way — as filters, not the whole story.\n\nSpecs will not tell you blister risk, late-run foam feel or whether a guidance system suits your gait. Try before you commit when you can, or buy somewhere returns are easy.","evidenceIds":["ev-racket-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-performance","heading":"Performance","body":"Versatile midplus Speed frame for players who want speed through the court.\n\nPerformance for the Head Speed MP 2024 should be read through intended use. Category-leading numbers in the wrong session still feel like a miss.\n\nWhere it is set up to perform\n• All-court versatility\n• Accessible handling\n\nWhere it is less convincing\n• Not the stiffest plow-through option\n\nBest performance fit: You want all-court versatility as a weekly priority — that is the Speed MP 2024's main job (Balanced beginner-to-intermediate option with room to grow); Most of your sessions line up with accessible handling more than an adjacent specialty role; Most of your sessions line up with approachable Speed geometry more than an adjacent specialty role.\n\nWeaker performance fit: You need to avoid not the stiffest plow-through option — forcing the Speed MP 2024 into that job usually disappoints.\n\nJudge it for the sessions it was built for. A race shoe will “win” a sprint feel test that a daily trainer was never meant to take — that does not make the trainer bad.","evidenceIds":["ev-racket-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-strengths","heading":"Where it is strongest","body":"I'd buy the Head Speed MP 2024 when these outcomes match what you need most weeks:\n\nWhat it does well\n• All-court versatility\n• Accessible handling\n\nThe standout is all-court versatility. If that is your main weekly need, keep going. If not, check trade-offs and alternatives.\n\nBest for: You want all-court versatility as a weekly priority — that is the Speed MP 2024's main job (Balanced beginner-to-intermediate option with room to grow); Most of your sessions line up with accessible handling more than an adjacent specialty role; Most of your sessions line up with approachable Speed geometry more than an adjacent specialty role.","evidenceIds":["ev-racket-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-tradeoffs","heading":"Trade-offs & limits","body":"The Head Speed MP 2024 is not trying to do every job. These are the compromises to weigh:\n\n• Not the stiffest plow-through option\n\nSkip it if: You need to avoid not the stiffest plow-through option — forcing the Speed MP 2024 into that job usually disappoints.\n\nThose limits matter when they hit your primary sessions — not when they only show up once a month. If your week sits outside this product's job, pick a peer built for that job instead.","evidenceIds":["ev-racket-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-usecase","heading":"Who it is for","body":"I'd buy the Head Speed MP 2024 when most of your weekly sessions match what it does well.\n\nBest when you want\n• You want all-court versatility as a weekly priority — that is the Speed MP 2024's main job (Balanced beginner-to-intermediate option with room to grow)\n• Most of your sessions line up with accessible handling more than an adjacent specialty role\n• Most of your sessions line up with approachable Speed geometry more than an adjacent specialty role\n• All-court versatility\n• Accessible handling\n\nLook elsewhere when\n• You need to avoid not the stiffest plow-through option — forcing the Speed MP 2024 into that job usually disappoints\n• Not the stiffest plow-through option\n\nIf more than half your week sits in the “look elsewhere” list, open the alternatives instead of forcing a compromise.","evidenceIds":["ev-racket-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-value","heading":"Value","body":"You are mainly paying for all-court versatility or accessible handling.\n\nYou are also accepting not the stiffest plow-through option — fine when that is not your weekly mix.\n\nStrongest value for: You want all-court versatility as a weekly priority — that is the Speed MP 2024's main job (Balanced beginner-to-intermediate option with room to grow); Most of your sessions line up with accessible handling more than an adjacent specialty role; Most of your sessions line up with approachable Speed geometry more than an adjacent specialty role.\n\nWeaker value for: You need to avoid not the stiffest plow-through option — forcing the Speed MP 2024 into that job usually disappoints.\n\nCheck live street price in the offers module. I'd pay the premium when the role is clear; otherwise compare the linked alternatives or a prior generation on sale.","evidenceIds":["ev-racket-editorial"]}],
