    sections: [{"id":"sec-overview","heading":"What it is","body":"Approachable folding treadmill for walking and jogging at home.\n\nHorizon Fitness T202 Treadmill is built for a specific job in the category — use that job as your first filter.\n\nI'd shortlist it when you want apartment-friendly fold or lower entry price band.\n\nI'd pause if not built for elite sprint intervals would show up often in your week.\n\nBottom line: Approachable folding treadmill for walking and jogging at home. I'd shortlist it when you want apartment-friendly fold. I'd pause if not built for elite sprint intervals shows up often in your week.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-wave24-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-verified-specs","heading":"Key specs","body":"Here are the numbers that matter for the Horizon Fitness T202 Treadmill:\n\n• Motorised: Yes\n• Foldable: Yes\n• Max User Weight: 136 kg\n• Max Speed: 16 km/h\n• Width: 850 mm\n• Depth: 1750 mm\n\nWeight and stack shape how protective or lively a shoe feels; drop and geometry change the transition; stability and terrain labels tell you the intended job; width options change who can wear it. For watches and other gear, treat battery, sensors and materials the same way — as filters, not the whole story.\n\nSpecs will not tell you blister risk, late-run foam feel or whether a guidance system suits your gait. Try before you commit when you can, or buy somewhere returns are easy.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-wave24-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-performance","heading":"Performance","body":"Approachable folding treadmill for walking and jogging at home.\n\nPerformance for the Horizon Fitness T202 Treadmill should be read through intended use. Category-leading numbers in the wrong session still feel like a miss.\n\nWhere it is set up to perform\n• Apartment-friendly fold\n• Lower entry price band\n\nWhere it is less convincing\n• Not built for elite sprint intervals\n\nBest performance fit: You want apartment-friendly fold as a weekly priority — that is the T202 Treadmill's main job; Most of your sessions line up with lower entry price band more than an adjacent specialty role; Most of your sessions line up with folding apartment option more than an adjacent specialty role.\n\nWeaker performance fit: You need to avoid not built for elite sprint intervals — forcing the T202 Treadmill into that job usually disappoints.\n\nJudge it for the sessions it was built for. A race shoe will “win” a sprint feel test that a daily trainer was never meant to take — that does not make the trainer bad.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-wave24-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-strengths","heading":"Where it is strongest","body":"I'd buy the Horizon Fitness T202 Treadmill when these outcomes match what you need most weeks:\n\nWhat it does well\n• Apartment-friendly fold\n• Lower entry price band\n\nThe standout is apartment-friendly fold. If that is your main weekly need, keep going. If not, check trade-offs and alternatives.\n\nBest for: You want apartment-friendly fold as a weekly priority — that is the T202 Treadmill's main job; Most of your sessions line up with lower entry price band more than an adjacent specialty role; Most of your sessions line up with folding apartment option more than an adjacent specialty role.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-wave24-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-tradeoffs","heading":"Trade-offs & limits","body":"The Horizon Fitness T202 Treadmill is not trying to do every job. These are the compromises to weigh:\n\n• Not built for elite sprint intervals\n\nSkip it if: You need to avoid not built for elite sprint intervals — forcing the T202 Treadmill into that job usually disappoints.\n\nThose limits matter when they hit your primary sessions — not when they only show up once a month. If your week sits outside this product's job, pick a peer built for that job instead.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-wave24-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-usecase","heading":"Who it is for","body":"I'd buy the Horizon Fitness T202 Treadmill when most of your weekly sessions match what it does well.\n\nBest when you want\n• You want apartment-friendly fold as a weekly priority — that is the T202 Treadmill's main job\n• Most of your sessions line up with lower entry price band more than an adjacent specialty role\n• Most of your sessions line up with folding apartment option more than an adjacent specialty role\n• Apartment-friendly fold\n• Lower entry price band\n\nLook elsewhere when\n• You need to avoid not built for elite sprint intervals — forcing the T202 Treadmill into that job usually disappoints\n• Not built for elite sprint intervals\n\nIf more than half your week sits in the “look elsewhere” list, open the alternatives instead of forcing a compromise.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-wave24-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-value","heading":"Value","body":"You are mainly paying for apartment-friendly fold or lower entry price band.\n\nYou are also accepting not built for elite sprint intervals — fine when that is not your weekly mix.\n\nStrongest value for: You want apartment-friendly fold as a weekly priority — that is the T202 Treadmill's main job; Most of your sessions line up with lower entry price band more than an adjacent specialty role; Most of your sessions line up with folding apartment option more than an adjacent specialty role.\n\nWeaker value for: You need to avoid not built for elite sprint intervals — forcing the T202 Treadmill into that job usually disappoints.\n\nCheck live street price in the offers module. I'd pay the premium when the role is clear; otherwise compare the linked alternatives or a prior generation on sale.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-wave24-editorial"]}],
