    sections: [{"id":"sec-overview","heading":"What it is","body":"Budget weighted vest for home conditioning and walk/run hybrids.\n\nMirafit Weighted Vest is built for a specific job in the category — use that job as your first filter.\n\nI'd shortlist it when you want affordable entry or eU availability.\n\nI'd pause if less premium materials would show up often in your week.\n\nBottom line: Budget weighted vest for home conditioning and walk/run hybrids. I'd shortlist it when you want affordable entry. I'd pause if less premium materials shows up often in your week.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial","ev-fitness-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-verified-specs","heading":"Key specs","body":"Here are the numbers that matter for the Mirafit Weighted Vest:\n\n• Adjustable: Yes\n\nWeight and stack shape how protective or lively a shoe feels; drop and geometry change the transition; stability and terrain labels tell you the intended job; width options change who can wear it. For watches and other gear, treat battery, sensors and materials the same way — as filters, not the whole story.\n\nSpecs will not tell you blister risk, late-run foam feel or whether a guidance system suits your gait. Try before you commit when you can, or buy somewhere returns are easy.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial","ev-fitness-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-performance","heading":"Performance","body":"Budget weighted vest for home conditioning and walk/run hybrids.\n\nPerformance for the Mirafit Weighted Vest should be read through intended use. Category-leading numbers in the wrong session still feel like a miss.\n\nWhere it is set up to perform\n• Affordable entry\n• EU availability\n\nWhere it is less convincing\n• Less premium materials\n\nBest performance fit: You want affordable entry as a weekly priority — that is the Weighted Vest's main job; Most of your sessions line up with eU availability more than an adjacent specialty role.\n\nWeaker performance fit: You need to avoid less premium materials — forcing the Weighted Vest into that job usually disappoints.\n\nJudge it for the sessions it was built for. A race shoe will “win” a sprint feel test that a daily trainer was never meant to take — that does not make the trainer bad.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial","ev-fitness-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-strengths","heading":"Where it is strongest","body":"I'd buy the Mirafit Weighted Vest when these outcomes match what you need most weeks:\n\nWhat it does well\n• Affordable entry\n• EU availability\n\nThe standout is affordable entry. If that is your main weekly need, keep going. If not, check trade-offs and alternatives.\n\nBest for: You want affordable entry as a weekly priority — that is the Weighted Vest's main job; Most of your sessions line up with eU availability more than an adjacent specialty role.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial","ev-fitness-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-tradeoffs","heading":"Trade-offs & limits","body":"The Mirafit Weighted Vest is not trying to do every job. These are the compromises to weigh:\n\n• Less premium materials\n\nSkip it if: You need to avoid less premium materials — forcing the Weighted Vest into that job usually disappoints.\n\nThose limits matter when they hit your primary sessions — not when they only show up once a month. If your week sits outside this product's job, pick a peer built for that job instead.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial","ev-fitness-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-usecase","heading":"Who it is for","body":"I'd buy the Mirafit Weighted Vest when most of your weekly sessions match what it does well.\n\nBest when you want\n• You want affordable entry as a weekly priority — that is the Weighted Vest's main job\n• Most of your sessions line up with eU availability more than an adjacent specialty role\n• Affordable entry\n• EU availability\n\nLook elsewhere when\n• You need to avoid less premium materials — forcing the Weighted Vest into that job usually disappoints\n• Less premium materials\n\nIf more than half your week sits in the “look elsewhere” list, open the alternatives instead of forcing a compromise.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial","ev-fitness-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-value","heading":"Value","body":"You are mainly paying for affordable entry or eU availability.\n\nYou are also accepting less premium materials — fine when that is not your weekly mix.\n\nStrongest value for: You want affordable entry as a weekly priority — that is the Weighted Vest's main job; Most of your sessions line up with eU availability more than an adjacent specialty role.\n\nWeaker value for: You need to avoid less premium materials — forcing the Weighted Vest into that job usually disappoints.\n\nCheck live street price in the offers module. I'd pay the premium when the role is clear; otherwise compare the linked alternatives or a prior generation on sale.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial","ev-fitness-editorial"]}],
