    sections: [{"id":"sec-overview","heading":"What it is","body":"Race-minimal NNormal vest for fast trail and ultra efforts — stripped storage for flasks and essentials when you refuse adventure-pack bulk.\n\nNNormal Race Vest is built for a specific job in the category — use that job as your first filter.\n\nI'd shortlist it when you want true race-minimal profile for fast mountain efforts, low weight keeps the focus on running, not packing or aligns with NNormal trail-racing ethos.\n\nI'd pause if little forgiveness for big jackets or adventure days or premium pricing for a deliberately small feature set would show up often in your week.\n\nBottom line: Race-minimal NNormal vest for fast trail and ultra efforts — stripped storage for flasks and essentials when you refuse adventure-pack bulk. I'd shortlist it when you want true race-minimal profile for fast mountain efforts. I'd pause if little forgiveness for big jackets or adventure days shows up often in your week.","evidenceIds":["ev-catalog-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-verified-specs","heading":"Key specs","body":"Here are the numbers that matter for the NNormal Race Vest:\n\n• Weight: 170 g\n• Capacity: 5 L\n• Included Flasks: 2\n• Included Flask Volume: 500 ml\n• Flask Pockets: 2\n• Reservoir Compatible: No\n• Reservoir Included: No\n• Total Hydration Capacity: 1000 ml\n• Bottle Capacity: 1000 ml\n• Bladder Compatible: No\n• Storage: Minimal race flask and stretch stash\n• Front Storage: Soft-flask sleeves\n\nWeight and stack shape how protective or lively a shoe feels; drop and geometry change the transition; stability and terrain labels tell you the intended job; width options change who can wear it. For watches and other gear, treat battery, sensors and materials the same way — as filters, not the whole story.\n\nSpecs will not tell you blister risk, late-run foam feel or whether a guidance system suits your gait. Try before you commit when you can, or buy somewhere returns are easy.","evidenceIds":["ev-catalog-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-performance","heading":"Performance","body":"Race-minimal NNormal vest for fast trail and ultra efforts — stripped storage for flasks and essentials when you refuse adventure-pack bulk.\n\nPerformance for the NNormal Race Vest should be read through intended use. Category-leading numbers in the wrong session still feel like a miss.\n\nWhere it is set up to perform\n• True race-minimal profile for fast mountain efforts\n• Low weight keeps the focus on running, not packing\n• Aligns with NNormal trail-racing ethos\n\nWhere it is less convincing\n• Little forgiveness for big jackets or adventure days\n• Premium pricing for a deliberately small feature set\n\nBest performance fit: You want true race-minimal profile for fast mountain efforts as a weekly priority — that is the Race Vest's main job (NNormal Race Vest for competitive trail race carry); Most of your sessions line up with low weight keeps the focus on running, not packing more than an adjacent specialty role; Most of your sessions line up with aligns with NNormal trail-racing ethos more than an adjacent specialty role.\n\nWeaker performance fit: You need to avoid little forgiveness for big jackets or adventure days — forcing the Race Vest into that job usually disappoints; You need to avoid premium pricing for a deliberately small feature set on this model.\n\nJudge it for the sessions it was built for. A race shoe will “win” a sprint feel test that a daily trainer was never meant to take — that does not make the trainer bad.","evidenceIds":["ev-catalog-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-strengths","heading":"Where it is strongest","body":"I'd buy the NNormal Race Vest when these outcomes match what you need most weeks:\n\nWhat it does well\n• True race-minimal profile for fast mountain efforts\n• Low weight keeps the focus on running, not packing\n• Aligns with NNormal trail-racing ethos\n\nThe standout is true race-minimal profile for fast mountain efforts. If that is your main weekly need, keep going. If not, check trade-offs and alternatives.\n\nBest for: You want true race-minimal profile for fast mountain efforts as a weekly priority — that is the Race Vest's main job (NNormal Race Vest for competitive trail race carry); Most of your sessions line up with low weight keeps the focus on running, not packing more than an adjacent specialty role; Most of your sessions line up with aligns with NNormal trail-racing ethos more than an adjacent specialty role.","evidenceIds":["ev-catalog-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-tradeoffs","heading":"Trade-offs & limits","body":"The NNormal Race Vest is not trying to do every job. These are the compromises to weigh:\n\n• Little forgiveness for big jackets or adventure days\n• Premium pricing for a deliberately small feature set\n\nSkip it if: You need to avoid little forgiveness for big jackets or adventure days — forcing the Race Vest into that job usually disappoints; You need to avoid premium pricing for a deliberately small feature set on this model.\n\nThose limits matter when they hit your primary sessions — not when they only show up once a month. If your week sits outside this product's job, pick a peer built for that job instead.","evidenceIds":["ev-catalog-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-usecase","heading":"Who it is for","body":"I'd buy the NNormal Race Vest when most of your weekly sessions match what it does well.\n\nBest when you want\n• You want true race-minimal profile for fast mountain efforts as a weekly priority — that is the Race Vest's main job (NNormal Race Vest for competitive trail race carry)\n• Most of your sessions line up with low weight keeps the focus on running, not packing more than an adjacent specialty role\n• Most of your sessions line up with aligns with NNormal trail-racing ethos more than an adjacent specialty role\n• True race-minimal profile for fast mountain efforts\n• Low weight keeps the focus on running, not packing\n• Aligns with NNormal trail-racing ethos\n\nLook elsewhere when\n• You need to avoid little forgiveness for big jackets or adventure days — forcing the Race Vest into that job usually disappoints\n• You need to avoid premium pricing for a deliberately small feature set on this model\n• Little forgiveness for big jackets or adventure days\n• Premium pricing for a deliberately small feature set\n\nIf more than half your week sits in the “look elsewhere” list, open the alternatives instead of forcing a compromise.","evidenceIds":["ev-catalog-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-value","heading":"Value","body":"You are mainly paying for true race-minimal profile for fast mountain efforts, low weight keeps the focus on running, not packing or aligns with NNormal trail-racing ethos.\n\nYou are also accepting little forgiveness for big jackets or adventure days or premium pricing for a deliberately small feature set — fine when that is not your weekly mix.\n\nStrongest value for: You want true race-minimal profile for fast mountain efforts as a weekly priority — that is the Race Vest's main job (NNormal Race Vest for competitive trail race carry); Most of your sessions line up with low weight keeps the focus on running, not packing more than an adjacent specialty role; Most of your sessions line up with aligns with NNormal trail-racing ethos more than an adjacent specialty role.\n\nWeaker value for: You need to avoid little forgiveness for big jackets or adventure days — forcing the Race Vest into that job usually disappoints; You need to avoid premium pricing for a deliberately small feature set on this model.\n\nCheck live street price in the offers module. I'd pay the premium when the role is clear; otherwise compare the linked alternatives or a prior generation on sale.","evidenceIds":["ev-catalog-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial"]}],
