    reviewType: "expert-research",
    bottomLine: "Compact outdoor Polar challenger with sapphire AMOLED, dual-frequency GPS, and full-color maps. I'd shortlist it when you want polar training/recovery analytics with outdoor maps. I'd pause if smartwatch battery (~7 days) shorter than Garmin/COROS peers shows up often in your week.",
    verdict: "Buy the Polar Grit X2 when its main job matches most of your week — not as a default for every session. It earns a look for polar training/recovery analytics with outdoor maps or sapphire AMOLED and dual-frequency GPS in a compact chassis. Look elsewhere if smartwatch battery (~7 days) shorter than Garmin/COROS peers.",
    score: 84,
    summary: "Compact outdoor Polar challenger with sapphire AMOLED, dual-frequency GPS, and full-color maps. I'd shortlist it when you want polar training/recovery analytics with outdoor maps. I'd pause if smartwatch battery (~7 days) shorter than Garmin/COROS peers shows up often in your week.",
    reviewerId: "author-kitletics-editorial",
