    sections: [{"id":"sec-overview","heading":"What it is","body":"Stiff power bar for squats, bench and deadlifts.\n\nRogue Ohio Power Bar is built for a specific job in the category — use that job as your first filter.\n\nI'd shortlist it when you want stiff shaft for heavy triples or aggressive power knurl.\n\nI'd pause if harsh for high-rep Olympic work would show up often in your week.\n\nBottom line: Stiff power bar for squats, bench and deadlifts. I'd shortlist it when you want stiff shaft for heavy triples. I'd pause if harsh for high-rep Olympic work shows up often in your week.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial","ev-fitness-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-verified-specs","heading":"Key specs","body":"Here are the numbers that matter for the Rogue Ohio Power Bar:\n\n• Length: 2200 mm\n• Shaft Diameter: 29 mm\n• Knurl Type: power\n\nWeight and stack shape how protective or lively a shoe feels; drop and geometry change the transition; stability and terrain labels tell you the intended job; width options change who can wear it. For watches and other gear, treat battery, sensors and materials the same way — as filters, not the whole story.\n\nSpecs will not tell you blister risk, late-run foam feel or whether a guidance system suits your gait. Try before you commit when you can, or buy somewhere returns are easy.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial","ev-fitness-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-performance","heading":"Performance","body":"Stiff power bar for squats, bench and deadlifts.\n\nPerformance for the Rogue Ohio Power Bar should be read through intended use. Category-leading numbers in the wrong session still feel like a miss.\n\nWhere it is set up to perform\n• Stiff shaft for heavy triples\n• Aggressive power knurl\n\nWhere it is less convincing\n• Harsh for high-rep Olympic work\n\nBest performance fit: You want stiff shaft for heavy triples as a weekly priority — that is the Ohio Power Bar's main job; Most of your sessions line up with aggressive power knurl more than an adjacent specialty role.\n\nWeaker performance fit: You need to avoid harsh for high-rep Olympic work — forcing the Ohio Power Bar into that job usually disappoints.\n\nJudge it for the sessions it was built for. A race shoe will “win” a sprint feel test that a daily trainer was never meant to take — that does not make the trainer bad.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial","ev-fitness-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-strengths","heading":"Where it is strongest","body":"I'd buy the Rogue Ohio Power Bar when these outcomes match what you need most weeks:\n\nWhat it does well\n• Stiff shaft for heavy triples\n• Aggressive power knurl\n\nThe standout is stiff shaft for heavy triples. If that is your main weekly need, keep going. If not, check trade-offs and alternatives.\n\nBest for: You want stiff shaft for heavy triples as a weekly priority — that is the Ohio Power Bar's main job; Most of your sessions line up with aggressive power knurl more than an adjacent specialty role.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial","ev-fitness-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-tradeoffs","heading":"Trade-offs & limits","body":"The Rogue Ohio Power Bar is not trying to do every job. These are the compromises to weigh:\n\n• Harsh for high-rep Olympic work\n\nSkip it if: You need to avoid harsh for high-rep Olympic work — forcing the Ohio Power Bar into that job usually disappoints.\n\nThose limits matter when they hit your primary sessions — not when they only show up once a month. If your week sits outside this product's job, pick a peer built for that job instead.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial","ev-fitness-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-usecase","heading":"Who it is for","body":"I'd buy the Rogue Ohio Power Bar when most of your weekly sessions match what it does well.\n\nBest when you want\n• You want stiff shaft for heavy triples as a weekly priority — that is the Ohio Power Bar's main job\n• Most of your sessions line up with aggressive power knurl more than an adjacent specialty role\n• Stiff shaft for heavy triples\n• Aggressive power knurl\n\nLook elsewhere when\n• You need to avoid harsh for high-rep Olympic work — forcing the Ohio Power Bar into that job usually disappoints\n• Harsh for high-rep Olympic work\n\nIf more than half your week sits in the “look elsewhere” list, open the alternatives instead of forcing a compromise.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial","ev-fitness-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-value","heading":"Value","body":"You are mainly paying for stiff shaft for heavy triples or aggressive power knurl.\n\nYou are also accepting harsh for high-rep Olympic work — fine when that is not your weekly mix.\n\nStrongest value for: You want stiff shaft for heavy triples as a weekly priority — that is the Ohio Power Bar's main job; Most of your sessions line up with aggressive power knurl more than an adjacent specialty role.\n\nWeaker value for: You need to avoid harsh for high-rep Olympic work — forcing the Ohio Power Bar into that job usually disappoints.\n\nCheck live street price in the offers module. I'd pay the premium when the role is clear; otherwise compare the linked alternatives or a prior generation on sale.","evidenceIds":["ev-fitness-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial","ev-fitness-editorial"]}],
