    reviewType: "expert-research",
    bottomLine: "12L race vest for trail and ultra hydration. I'd shortlist it when you want stable race fit across long trail days. I'd pause if overkill for road 10K shows up often in your week.",
    verdict: "Buy the Salomon ADV Skin 12 when its main job matches most of your week — not as a default for every session. It earns a look for stable race fit across long trail days or enough volume for mandatory ultra kit. Look elsewhere if overkill for road 10K.",
    score: 90,
    summary: "12L race vest for trail and ultra hydration. I'd shortlist it when you want stable race fit across long trail days. I'd pause if overkill for road 10K shows up often in your week.",
    reviewerId: "author-kitletics-editorial",
    testingContext: "We put this guide together from published specs and similar products in the same job. We have not personally tested this product unless the page says we did. Scores are meant to help you decide — affiliate links do not change the verdict.",
    editorialDisclosure: "No brand-supplied product or sponsored testing applied to this review unless stated. Affiliate availability does not affect scores or verdict.",
    sections: [{"id":"sec-overview","heading":"What it is","body":"12L race vest for trail and ultra hydration.\n\nSalomon ADV Skin 12 is built for a specific job in the category — use that job as your first filter.\n\nI'd shortlist it when you want stable race fit across long trail days or enough volume for mandatory ultra kit.\n\nI'd pause if overkill for road 10K or learning curve to pack pockets efficiently would show up often in your week.\n\nBottom line: 12L race vest for trail and ultra hydration. I'd shortlist it when you want stable race fit across long trail days. I'd pause if overkill for road 10K shows up often in your week.","evidenceIds":["ev-catalog-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-verified-specs","heading":"Key specs","body":"Here are the numbers that matter for the Salomon ADV Skin 12:\n\n• Weight: 270 g\n• Capacity: 12 L\n• Included Flasks: 2\n• Included Flask Volume: 500 ml\n• Flask Pockets: 2\n• Reservoir Compatible: Yes\n• Reservoir Included: No\n• Total Hydration Capacity: 2500 ml\n• Bladder Compatible: Yes\n• Bottle Capacity: 1000 ml\n• Storage: Multiple front and rear pockets for flasks, gels and mandatory kit\n• Front Storage: Twin soft-flask pockets + stretch snack pockets\n\nWeight and stack shape how protective or lively a shoe feels; drop and geometry change the transition; stability and terrain labels tell you the intended job; width options change who can wear it. For watches and other gear, treat battery, sensors and materials the same way — as filters, not the whole story.\n\nSpecs will not tell you blister risk, late-run foam feel or whether a guidance system suits your gait. Try before you commit when you can, or buy somewhere returns are easy.","evidenceIds":["ev-catalog-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-performance","heading":"Performance","body":"12L race vest for trail and ultra hydration.\n\nPerformance for the Salomon ADV Skin 12 should be read through intended use. Category-leading numbers in the wrong session still feel like a miss.\n\nWhere it is set up to perform\n• Stable race fit across long trail days\n• Enough volume for mandatory ultra kit\n\nWhere it is less convincing\n• Overkill for road 10K\n• Learning curve to pack pockets efficiently\n\nBest performance fit: You want stable race fit across long trail days as a weekly priority — that is the ADV Skin 12's main job; Most of your sessions line up with enough volume for mandatory ultra kit more than an adjacent specialty role; Most of your sessions line up with high trail/ultra capacity more than an adjacent specialty role.\n\nWeaker performance fit: You need to avoid overkill for road 10K — forcing the ADV Skin 12 into that job usually disappoints; You need to avoid learning curve to pack pockets efficiently on this model.\n\nJudge it for the sessions it was built for. A race shoe will “win” a sprint feel test that a daily trainer was never meant to take — that does not make the trainer bad.","evidenceIds":["ev-catalog-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-strengths","heading":"Where it is strongest","body":"I'd buy the Salomon ADV Skin 12 when these outcomes match what you need most weeks:\n\nWhat it does well\n• Stable race fit across long trail days\n• Enough volume for mandatory ultra kit\n\nThe standout is stable race fit across long trail days. If that is your main weekly need, keep going. If not, check trade-offs and alternatives.\n\nBest for: You want stable race fit across long trail days as a weekly priority — that is the ADV Skin 12's main job; Most of your sessions line up with enough volume for mandatory ultra kit more than an adjacent specialty role; Most of your sessions line up with high trail/ultra capacity more than an adjacent specialty role.","evidenceIds":["ev-catalog-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-tradeoffs","heading":"Trade-offs & limits","body":"The Salomon ADV Skin 12 is not trying to do every job. These are the compromises to weigh:\n\n• Overkill for road 10K\n• Learning curve to pack pockets efficiently\n\nSkip it if: You need to avoid overkill for road 10K — forcing the ADV Skin 12 into that job usually disappoints; You need to avoid learning curve to pack pockets efficiently on this model.\n\nThose limits matter when they hit your primary sessions — not when they only show up once a month. If your week sits outside this product's job, pick a peer built for that job instead.","evidenceIds":["ev-catalog-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-usecase","heading":"Who it is for","body":"I'd buy the Salomon ADV Skin 12 when most of your weekly sessions match what it does well.\n\nBest when you want\n• You want stable race fit across long trail days as a weekly priority — that is the ADV Skin 12's main job\n• Most of your sessions line up with enough volume for mandatory ultra kit more than an adjacent specialty role\n• Most of your sessions line up with high trail/ultra capacity more than an adjacent specialty role\n• Stable race fit across long trail days\n• Enough volume for mandatory ultra kit\n\nLook elsewhere when\n• You need to avoid overkill for road 10K — forcing the ADV Skin 12 into that job usually disappoints\n• You need to avoid learning curve to pack pockets efficiently on this model\n• Overkill for road 10K\n• Learning curve to pack pockets efficiently\n\nIf more than half your week sits in the “look elsewhere” list, open the alternatives instead of forcing a compromise.","evidenceIds":["ev-catalog-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial"]},{"id":"sec-value","heading":"Value","body":"You are mainly paying for stable race fit across long trail days or enough volume for mandatory ultra kit.\n\nYou are also accepting overkill for road 10K or learning curve to pack pockets efficiently — fine when that is not your weekly mix.\n\nStrongest value for: You want stable race fit across long trail days as a weekly priority — that is the ADV Skin 12's main job; Most of your sessions line up with enough volume for mandatory ultra kit more than an adjacent specialty role; Most of your sessions line up with high trail/ultra capacity more than an adjacent specialty role.\n\nWeaker value for: You need to avoid overkill for road 10K — forcing the ADV Skin 12 into that job usually disappoints; You need to avoid learning curve to pack pockets efficiently on this model.\n\nCheck live street price in the offers module. I'd pay the premium when the role is clear; otherwise compare the linked alternatives or a prior generation on sale.","evidenceIds":["ev-catalog-mfr","ev-catalog-editorial"]}],
