    title: "Salomon ADV Skin 5 Review",
    reviewType: "expert-research",
    bottomLine: "5L race vest with twin 500 ml soft flasks — enough for gels, phone and jacket without the ADV Skin 12 bulk; trades rear volume for a lighter bounce-controlled fit on trail, ultra and road longs. I'd shortlist it when you want stable Salomon Sensifit race harness with low bounce. I'd pause if no reservoir sleeve — bladder days need a larger ADV Skin or adventure vest shows up often in your week.",
    verdict: "Buy the Salomon ADV Skin 5 when its main job matches most of your week — not as a default for every session. It earns a look for stable Salomon Sensifit race harness with low bounce or twin 500 ml flasks cover most long-run hydration without a bladder. Look elsewhere if no reservoir sleeve — bladder days need a larger ADV Skin or adventure vest.",
